Here's the plan for how tools will move in and out of the bus.

- Every tool gets its own ID and a short story: what it is, where it's been.
- Check one out by scanning it with your phone. Log the kit and its condition, and it's yours for a week.
- Only one person borrows a tool at a time. No double-booking.
- Bring it back and we check it against what went out. Clean, and it's free for the next person.
- Damaged or missing pieces send it to repair instead of back on the shelf.
- None of this charges you automatically. A late tool gets a reminder, not a bill.
- First pilot: about ten sewing tools, before this opens up wider.
- Not live yet. This is the plan, being built and tested now.
